From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Place native tray menus above shell panels.

Noctalia panels use the TOP layer with exclusive keyboard interactivity.
Our native SNI menus also use TOP, with ON_DEMAND keyboard interactivity
since 0059. Niri prefers exclusive focus within a layer, so an open panel
can prevent the menu from receiving keyboard focus at all. Clicking an
unrelated application then produces no keyboard-leave event for Wine to
dismiss the menu.

Use OVERLAY for tray menus, keeping notifications on TOP. In Niri this
lets the newly mapped on-demand menu receive focus above a TOP panel.
Keep ON_DEMAND unchanged: clicks may move focus to another client and
trigger our existing dismissal path. Do not reintroduce exclusive grabs,
input-catcher windows, or repeated focus requests during redraw.

This does not guarantee initial focus on every compositor or override
another client's explicit popup grab. An exclusive OVERLAY-layer launcher
also still takes precedence; its host must release that focus before
handing off to an external menu. It addresses the TOP-layer focus priority
conflict, not every Noctalia launcher configuration. The report still
needs runtime confirmation with the affected shell version.

Follow-up to Erhan Bilgili (nanomatters)'s native SNI menu support from
https://github.com/nanomatters/wine-wineland.

Related: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/803#issuecomment-5890703475
References: https://github.com/niri-wm/niri/blob/main/src/niri.rs
References: https://github.com/niri-wm/niri/blob/main/src/handlers/layer_shell.rs
References: https://github.com/noctalia-dev/noctalia-shell/blob/legacy-v4/Modules/MainScreen/MainScreen.qml
---

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -2045,10 +2045,14 @@
     surface->role = WAYLAND_SURFACE_ROLE_LAYER;
     surface->layer_output = output;
     surface->layer_menu = menu;
+    /* Tray menus must be above top-layer panels with exclusive focus.
+     * Keep their keyboard interactivity non-exclusive so outside clicks can
+     * still move focus away and dismiss the menu. */
     surface->zwlr_layer_surface_v1 =
         zwlr_layer_shell_v1_get_layer_surface(process_wayland.zwlr_layer_shell_v1,
                                               surface->wl_surface, output,
-                                              ZWLR_LAYER_SHELL_V1_LAYER_TOP,
+                                              menu ? ZWLR_LAYER_SHELL_V1_LAYER_OVERLAY :
+                                                     ZWLR_LAYER_SHELL_V1_LAYER_TOP,
                                               menu ? "wine-menu" : "wine-notification");
     if (!surface->zwlr_layer_surface_v1) goto err;
 
